a somber ceremony for a country in this  array  a year after president jovenel moyes was  assassinated haitian authorities and  diplomats met to mark the occasion  current acting president ariel henry  says he's committed to seeking justice  i'm determined to encourage the  continuation of the investigation until  its conclusion haitian justice can count  on the unconditional support of the  government despite its weaknesses the  justice system must continue to track  down and sentence the culprits so that  our country will never have to go  through such drama again  but despite dozens of arrests including  a group of colombian mercenaries haiti's  investigation remained stalled and many  accuse henry himself of being involved  after he fired his justice minister and  a prosecutor last year when they called  for him to be investigated in connection  with the murder  he denies any involvement  on thursday hundreds took to the streets  of the capital porto prince in protest  burning tires and calling for henry's  resignation the prime minister must go  to jail because he was involved in the  killing of the president this is not  normal in the 21st century it is  shocking but his legacy will not die we  will continue  [Music]  some of the arrested colombian  mercenaries have released a video saying  they had gone over 70 hours without food  they haven't been charged and haven't  had access to a lawyer for 10 months  a separate investigation in the u.s has  led to three arrests including a former  u.s government criminal informant  in a statement on thursday u.s secretary  of state anthony blinken said the u.s  remains concerned about the limited  progress of haiti's investigation  since the killing the already fragile  economic and political situation in the  country fell deeper into this function  as gangs took over large parts of the  capital  thousands of people have been killed  tortured or forced to leave  well what has happened in haiti for the  past years shows that shortcuts do not  work there is a crisis it's getting  worse so we need to tackle the issues we  need to make sure that we fight gang  violence and have a political consensus  and have free election  but when none of these options on the  horizon haitians are left in a grim  spiral of violence and impunity that  sees an ever growing number of them  ready to risk their life to leave the  country alessandro  al-jazeera
 

